# An unparenthesized `@` chain has no fixed association: the checker picks the
# cheapest one from the shapes (here O(n^2) instead of O(n^3)), and `--explain`
# says what it saved. Parentheses the user wrote are respected: `y` is
# written in the O(n^3) order on purpose, so nothing is rewritten there.
A: Matrix[500, 500]
B: Matrix[500, 500]
C: Matrix[500, 500]
v: Vector[500]
x = A @ B @ C @ v
y = ((A @ B) @ C) @ v
print(x, y)
